# halal-competitions — core rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for architecture, data model, and commands.

## Scope & safety

- Small, focused diffs only — no drive-by refactors or mass upgrades
- Do **not** upgrade Firebase or Vuex without explicit user approval
- Planned upgrades live in `UPGRADES-TODO.md` — reference, don't execute, unless asked

## Patterns to follow

- Vuex: modular stores in `src/store/`; namespaced modules use `Module/action` dispatch syntax
- Paths: use `@/` alias for imports from `src/`
- Styling: Tailwind utility classes; match existing spacing/shadow patterns
- Data: competition definitions in `src/data.js` — don't duplicate counter ids elsewhere
- Week logic: Monday–Sunday via `dateRange()` / `dateRangeLastWeek()` in `utils.js`

## After changes

```bash
npm run lint
npm run test:unit   # when touching tested areas
```

## Reuse first

Check `src/composables/`, `components/shared/Base*`, and existing store actions before adding new abstractions.
